upx_packed_pe_x86_64.exe -- the win64/pe (PE32+) fixture for `kuna unpack` /
`kuna_analysis::upx::pe`, and the witness of issue #1294.

What it is
  The issue's own reproducer: three tiny functions linked with no CRT, packed by
  UPX 5.2.1 with default settings. 2,048 bytes packed; 3,072 bytes unpacked. The
  UPX! PackHeader is in the header padding at 0x1fd and reads version=13,
  format=36 (win64/pe), method=2 (NRV2B_LE32), level=8, filter=0x49 (ctok32).
  One compressed block, 0x11d bytes in, 0x41ac out. No imports, no relocations
  (none are needed), an exception directory (.pdata).

  Before the fix `kuna unpack` answered it with "corrupt UPX image: PackHeader
  declares an overlay outside the file": the PE header parser rejected PE32+, and
  the tail-scan fallback then decoded the PE PackHeader as if it had the overlay
  field only non-PE targets carry.

  `upx -d` (5.2.1 and 5.3.0) writes the same 3,072 bytes `kuna unpack` does. Both
  differ from the linker's original only in the .text padding past the section's
  virtual size (0x7b), which UPX never compresses and so writes back as zeros.

Where it came from
  Built in the mstorsjo/llvm-mingw docker image (clang 23.1.4, lld-link), exactly
  as the issue gives it:

      cat > fixture.c <<'C'
      volatile int global_counter = 5;
      __declspec(noinline) int increment(int n) { return n + global_counter; }
      __declspec(noinline) int select_value(int n) { return n > 0 ? increment(n) : -1; }
      void entry(void) { volatile int r = select_value(7); (void)r; }
      C
      clang -target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc -c fixture.c -o fixture.obj
      lld-link /entry:entry /subsystem:console /nodefaultlib /out:fixture.exe fixture.obj
      upx -o upx_packed_pe_x86_64.exe fixture.exe          # UPX 5.2.1

  sha256(original fixture.exe)  e79c2e177ec3737e41c56bd4757bf3c8203ddd174d60d80b0d0b291a5b7607d9
  sha256(packed)                642cb05761d02a637a334a78798022f4cf135c307c59c41b36a3d0c2f903aefb

Why it is vendored rather than built
  `upx` is not a build dependency of this repo and is not installed on CI, and no
  CI toolchain links a PE32+.
